abstract: >-
  A self-directed curriculum of 16 units plus an optional capstone, for
  pragmatic mastery of distributed and data-intensive systems. Covers
  storage engines and the cost of a write, batch and stream processing,
  partitioning and the shuffle, vectorized query execution and physical
  planning, distributed model training and parallelism strategies,
  attention and cache-aware inference routing, distributed snapshots,
  and Kubernetes operators with production observability. Roughly half
  the units build a mechanism from primitives; the rest drive a real
  engine (Spark, Flink, DuckDB, Kubeflow) until it fails instructively.
  Each system is driven in the language that system is actually written
  and used in, so the curriculum spans Python, Java, and Go rather than
  standardising on one.
